{"track":"addmath","num":"8.01","title":"Integration & Kinematics","sub":null,"sections":[{"heading":"Integration & Kinematics Practice Exercises","questions":[{"q":"Evaluate the definite integral: \\( \\int_0^1 (2x + 1)^3 \\, dx \\).","choices":["\\( \\frac{80}{2} \\)","\\( \\frac{84}{8} \\)","\\( \\frac{80}{4} \\)","\\( \\frac{80}{8} \\)"],"correct":3,"answer":"Substitute \\( u = 2x + 1 \\implies du = 2\\,dx \\). Integral: \\( \\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\frac{u^4}{4}\\right]_1^{3} = \\frac{(3)^4 - 1^{4}}{8} = \\frac{80}{8} \\). [M1][A1]","figure":{"type":"fn","xrange":[-5,5],"yrange":[-5,7],"fns":[{"fn":"(x - (0))*(x - (0)) + (-1)","color":"var(--fig-indigo)","label":"y = f(x)"},{"fn":"2*x - 4","color":"var(--fig-amber)","dash":"4,4","label":"y = g(x)"}],"points":[{"x":0,"y":-1,"label":"(0, -1)"}]}},{"q":"Evaluate the definite integral: \\( \\int_0^1 (3x + 1)^3 \\, dx \\).","choices":["\\( \\frac{255}{4} \\)","\\( \\frac{255}{3} \\)","\\( \\frac{259}{12} \\)","\\( \\frac{255}{12} \\)"],"correct":3,"answer":"Substitute \\( u = 3x + 1 \\implies du = 3\\,dx \\). Integral: \\( \\frac{1}{3}\\left[\\frac{u^4}{4}\\right]_1^{4} = \\frac{(4)^4 - 1^{4}}{12} = \\frac{255}{12} \\). [M1][A1]"},{"q":"Evaluate the definite integral: \\( \\int_0^1 (4x + 1)^3 \\, dx \\).","choices":["\\( \\frac{625}{16} \\)","\\( \\frac{624}{4} \\)","\\( \\frac{628}{16} \\)","\\( \\frac{624}{16} \\)"],"correct":3,"answer":"Substitute \\( u = 4x + 1 \\implies du = 4\\,dx \\). Integral: \\( \\frac{1}{4}\\left[\\frac{u^4}{4}\\right]_1^{5} = \\frac{(5)^4 - 1^{4}}{16} = \\frac{624}{16} \\). [M1][A1]","figure":{"type":"fn","xrange":[-5,5],"yrange":[-5,7],"fns":[{"fn":"(x - (-1))*(x - (-1)) + (1)","color":"var(--fig-indigo)","label":"y = f(x)"},{"fn":"4*x - 5","color":"var(--fig-amber)","dash":"4,4","label":"y = g(x)"}],"points":[{"x":-1,"y":1,"label":"(-1, 1)"}]}},{"q":"Evaluate the definite integral: \\( \\int_0^1 (5x + 1)^3 \\, dx \\).","choices":["\\( \\frac{1295}{5} \\)","\\( \\frac{1295}{4} \\)","\\( \\fr